From 7b12cdb5b8f368ae34d7bde8ee8b87b92016e86c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nusage <dev@nusage>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:14:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add Nushell support

A profile for Nushell scripts and modules (*.nu) and NUON data (*.nuon), with
the tree-sitter-nu grammar.

Nushell predeclares the defs and externs of a block, so they commute, keyed
by name. Whole use statements remain ordered: imports can shadow the same
command name, so combining concurrent imports could silently select one
side. Tests cover those collisions at the top level and inside a block;
even additions importing distinct names at the same position stay a conflict.

Record entries commute, keyed by their key, with spreads kept in place.
The named commands within one use statement commute too. Lists, tables,
pipelines, match arms and command parameters keep their order. Strings,
interpolated strings and the shebang are merged as a whole.

The grammar hides separators between entries, so concurrent record additions
use a newline separator; a formatter puts an inline record back on one line.
